  concept: "Authored objective: Bridge Balance (MID A - MID B).\nAuthored requirement:
    Measure the magnitude of voltage between the two divider midpoints; keep below
    0.05 V. voltage \u2264 0.05 V. Connection pair R_LBOTTOM_Input and R_RBOTTOM_Input.\nGeneral
    teaching principle: Bridge measurements compare relevant branch conditions and
    reference points; balance must be verified rather than assumed.\nOnly fresh,
    authoritative game evidence can establish that this objective is complete."
  analogy: Comparing two scales is useful only when both use compatible reference
    points.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: A single matching midpoint voltage is not always sufficient to establish
    a healthy bridge.
